{#- Model card: the X learner. The body is shared with the T learner in cards/_uplift.md.j2. -#}
{% import '_macros.j2' as m %}
{% set card = 'uplift-x-learner' %}
{% set learner = 'x_learner' %}
{% set learner_name = 'X learner' %}
{% set reads = namespace(ahead_of_t=false, level_with_rule=false) %}
{% for row in manifest.tables['targeting.criteo.qini_differences'].rows %}
{% if row[0] == 'T learner minus X learner' and row[3] < 0 %}{% set reads.ahead_of_t = true %}{% endif %}
{% if row[0] == 'X learner minus Sure things' and row[2] < 0 < row[3] %}{% set reads.level_with_rule = true %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% set method %}
The X learner is the two stage learner of Kunzel, Sekhon, Bickel and Yu
(`marginal_targeting.learners.XLearner`). Stage one fits an outcome model per arm, as the T learner
does. Each customer then gets an imputed effect from the other arm's model: a contacted customer's
outcome less what the no contact model predicts for them, and the contact model's prediction for an
uncontacted customer less that customer's outcome. Stage two regresses the imputed effects on the
features, once per arm, and blends the two effect models with the propensity score as the weight;
because assignment is randomized, the propensity is the contacted share of the training split.
{% endset %}
{% set weakness %}
{% call m.holds(reads.ahead_of_t and reads.level_with_rule and raw('targeting.sim.pehe.x_learner') < raw('targeting.sim.pehe.t_learner'), 'that the X learner leads the T learner and ties the rule on Criteo') %}
Its score rests on imputed effects, which carry the errors of the stage one outcome models into
stage two; where those models are poor, as on Hillstrom's few features, the imputations are poor
too. It is the better of the two learners where there is signal: on the simulator its PEHE is
{{ v('targeting.sim.pehe.x_learner') }} against the T learner's {{ v('targeting.sim.pehe.t_learner') }},
and on Criteo the paired difference puts it ahead of the T learner, while it cannot be told apart
from the sure things rule.
{% endcall %}
{% endset %}
